      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's true that when the perceived foundations crumble, simple coping mechanisms can feel utterly inadequate. You are naming a profound existential crisis about the nature of reality itself, which is terrifying. Instead of fighting the fall completely, can you allow yourself to observe the dust without immediately needing to rebuild a perfect structure? Sometimes the honesty is found not in clinging to what was, but in bravely exploring what remains when everything familiar has fallen away.",
      "source": "target",
